WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.020
Protect people: their data, your voice, and respect at work.

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.830
This is the video for module three of Ethics and Accountability at Work.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:21.060
Personal data is any information that identifies a living person: a name with a phone number, an address, a photo, a BVN, bank details or health information.

4
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:30.950
In Nigeria, the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 sets the rules, and the Nigeria Data Protection Commission enforces them.

5
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:40.540
Before you share anyone's data, ask four questions. Do they need it? Is this the purpose? Is it the minimum? Is the channel secure?

6
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.590
And never post personal details, debts or health information in a group chat.

7
00:00:46.840 --> 00:01:00.230
For example, Joy is secretary of a 60-member thrift and credit society in Owerri. The chairperson asks her to post the defaulters, with amounts and phone numbers, on the WhatsApp group to shame them into paying.

8
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:08.430
Joy runs the checklist. Do all 60 members need this? No. Is shaming the purpose the data was collected for? No.

9
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:22.210
So she suggests private messages to each defaulter, with the amount and the agreed repayment date. The group hears only totals: 420,000 naira outstanding across 7 loans.

10
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.060
The full list stays in a password-protected sheet shared only with the treasurer and chairperson.

11
00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:44.410
A breach is when personal data is lost, stolen, or shared with the wrong people, like a spreadsheet sent to the wrong WhatsApp group. First, contain it. Delete the message for everyone, remove link access, or change the password.

12
00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.460
Tell your manager or the person responsible for data immediately, in writing.

13
00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.700
Write down what data was involved and how many people are affected.

14
00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:07.680
Under the Act, organisations must notify the Commission within 72 hours of a breach likely to pose a high risk to people. Hiding it only makes it worse.

15
00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:17.940
Speaking up means raising a concern about wrongdoing that affects others. First, write down what you saw, with dates, amounts and who was present.

16
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:31.240
For example, Esther works in accounts at an NGO in Jos. The same supplier invoice for 1,200,000 naira has been paid twice. She does not assume fraud. It could be an error.

17
00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:38.970
Start at the lowest safe level. Esther emails the facts to her finance manager, who is not involved.

18
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:47.070
Nothing happens for three weeks. She follows up once, then uses the next level in her organisation's policy.

19
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:56.720
The policy names the board audit committee chair, so she sends the same calm summary there, marked confidential. The money is recovered.

20
00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:10.450
For criminal matters or public money, external bodies such as the EFCC and ICPC exist. Never post accusations on social media. And if you fear for your physical safety, put that first.

21
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:22.630
Everyone has the right to work without being humiliated, threatened or pressured. The key word is unwanted. Meant as a joke is no excuse. What matters is the effect.

22
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:31.810
Quid pro quo means this for that: when a promotion, a contract or a loan approval is made to depend on a sexual favour.

23
00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:42.540
A hostile environment is created by repeated sexual jokes, comments on a woman's body, or explicit images in the office WhatsApp group.

24
00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:59.150
Bullying is repeated intimidation: shouting at someone in front of customers, or mocking her accent or tribe. If it happens to you, write down each incident, screenshot messages, and report in writing. You are not to blame.

25
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:06.540
When you see someone being harassed, you can help without putting yourself in danger. Use the 5Ds.

26
00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:12.270
Distract. For example: Madam Ada, the customer is asking for you.

27
00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.590
Delegate. Get a supervisor, security staff or the chairperson.

28
00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:25.990
Document. If it is safe, note what happens and give it to the person affected. Never post it without her permission.

29
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.000
Delay. Afterwards, ask her: are you okay? How can I help?

30
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:42.080
Direct. If it is safe, say briefly: that is not okay. And remember, punishing anyone for a complaint made in good faith is itself serious misconduct.

31
00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:55.360
Your practice. Map every place you keep other people's data, and fix one weak point today. Fill in your escalation ladder with names or roles, and write a short factual practice report.

32
00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:01.660
Then plan one 5D action for a place you work or meet. Now continue with the lessons below.
